## Summary

The paper contributes a modular reinforcement learning architecture where brain-like replay emerges naturally from task optimization and specific HF-PFC communication constraints, avoiding hard-coded replay buffers. The single most important piece of evidence delivering on this contribution is found in Section 3.1 (Figure 2E), where the temporal evolution of the model's replay distribution during a task switch quantitatively mirrors biological data from Igata et al. (2021) (Figure 2C), specifically validating the proposed emergence conditions through the pre-adoption increase of shortcut segment replay.

