## Novel Insights
The paper's core insight—that naive fusion of OSR and multimodal methods degrades performance due to over-compression of feature representations—is empirically demonstrated but not deeply analyzed. The "fusion degradation" phenomenon is a useful observation for the multimodal OSR community, though similar degradation patterns have been noted in other multimodal contexts (e.g., "confidence degradation" in MultiMisD, "magnitude collapse" in OSR interaction studies). The MRN architecture itself uses standard components (cross-attention, MoE) without novel theoretical contributions. The insight is practical but not fundamentally novel beyond the paper's own contributions.

