2. **Performance Improvement Under Sparsity**: Experimental results in Table 1 demonstrate that the proposed method achieves a +1.18% accuracy gain on CIFAR10 relative to non-sparse baselines, whereas competing sparse methods like Grad R and ESLSNN report accuracy degradation (-0.30% and -1.7% respectively), indicating superior generalization capability despite compression (Section 4.2).
