## Summary

The paper contributes Gradient Storm, a backdoor attack technique that utilizes expanded parameter space coverage to inject multiple, robust triggers into neural networks with minimal data perturbation. The single most important piece of evidence that it delivers on this contribution is Table 1, which demonstrates that Gradient Storm achieves a 99.76% Attack Success Rate on CIFAR-10, significantly surpassing the prior state-of-the-art Sleeper Agent attack (89.73%) while preserving equivalent Benign Accuracy.

